WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
INTRO:
With all the high inflation and rate hikes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:07.120
that we’ve been seeing over past several months,&nbsp;
I’m sure you’ve all heard about the threat of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.720
recession looming around the corner. While the&nbsp;
media often makes a big fuss about recessions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.720
a recession is simply 2 consecutive quarters of&nbsp;
GDP decline. In western countries, we usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:26.080
see a GDP contraction of 2 to 3% and this turns&nbsp;
into international fear. But, one notable region&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.760
has not only been seeing a recession but a full&nbsp;
on depression and the world has barely noticed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:42.560
Macao’s GDP is not down 5, 10, or even 20%.&nbsp;
Macao’s GDP is down an eyewatering 56.3%.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:49.200
If this was the US, we’d probably see negative&nbsp;
interest rates and $20,000 stimulus checks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.720
but China hasn’t really done anything about&nbsp;
it. In fact, China has only made things worse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.680
by cracking down on gambling. Hearing this, I&nbsp;
don’t think you’d be surprised to heard that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.480
Macau’s casinos were already bleeding hundreds of&nbsp;
millions per month throughout the past two years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.560
Things have only gotten worse with&nbsp;
the recent surge in Covid cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:14.560
which has resulted in all Macau casinos shutting&nbsp;
down completely. And given that 80% of government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.000
revenue comes from casino taxes, there’s no&nbsp;
question that the entire region is on edge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.840
So, how much longer do we have until&nbsp;
Macau’s economy becomes unsalvageable.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.520
SURVIVE WITHOUT GAMBLING:&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.720
To gauge Macau’s economic health, we first have&nbsp;
to look into whether Macau can survive without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.640
gambling. Of course, they’re extremely dependent&nbsp;
on gambling right now, but can this be changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.840
over the next several years? Well, according to&nbsp;
many experts and even casino owners, the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.120
is a resounding no. Professor Glenn McCartney from&nbsp;
the Univeristy of Macau for example suggests the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.640
following. "Given that we didn't diversify for&nbsp;
20 years. It isn't going to happen tomorrow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:02.960
There's no quick fix." Similarly, a casino owner&nbsp;
named Lawrence Ho says “As bad as it sounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.240
I don’t think there’s a future for just a pure&nbsp;
non-gaming resort in Macau,” “The truth is:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.360
gaming is really the financial engine,” “Yes,&nbsp;
you can have these great integrated resorts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.280
but without the gaming component the math doesn’t&nbsp;
work.” Obviously, these are not he most reassuring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.280
comments, but how did things even get so bad in&nbsp;
the first place? Well, to answer this, we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.880
to look at how Macau become the Asian Las Vegas in&nbsp;
the first place. Taking a look back, the history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.080
of Macau’s gambling roots stretch all the way back&nbsp;
to 1557 when the Portuguese took over the region.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:41.760
At the time, the Chinese called the region “A Ma&nbsp;
Gao” which means bay of the goddess of sailors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.880
The Portuguese adapted this name into Macau and&nbsp;
with that they opened up the first European colony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:53.200
in East Asia. For the first 100 years, the region&nbsp;
thrived as an international shipping hub. Macau&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.240
was the perfect intermediary between Asia and&nbsp;
the western super powers, but all of this would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:04.080
change in the early 1800s. You see, after the&nbsp;
British won the 1814 Opuim War against China,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.520
the British and the Dutch would take control&nbsp;
of the trading routes between Europe and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:13.280
China. And this made Macau basically irrelevant&nbsp;
overnight. Macau still played a large role when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.640
came to religion, housing refugees, and culture,&nbsp;
but none of these factors helped the economy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.840
Desperate for new modes of revenue, the&nbsp;
Portuguese legalized a slew of activities in 1840s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:30.080
one of which was gambling. Gambling was socially&nbsp;
taboo across much of Asia at the time and it still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:35.920
very much is. Nonetheless, Macau was able to&nbsp;
attract quite a few visitors. By the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.960
century, gambling became one of the top revenue&nbsp;
sources for the region, but it still wasn’t the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.680
dominant source. You see, most of the gambling&nbsp;
houses that popped up throughout the first 100&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.960
years were pretty conservative. In other words,&nbsp;
players actually had a decent chance of winning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:57.040
Of course, the odds were still stacked in the&nbsp;
casino’s favor, but we saw odds of 55-45 or 60-40.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:03.840
This was good for gambler’s wallets, but it&nbsp;
wasn’t the best for Macau’s bottomline. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.920
all of this would change in 1962 when Macau&nbsp;
granted monopoly rights to all forms of gambling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:13.840
to a man named Stanley Ho. Stanley was a ruthless&nbsp;
businessman who saw insane opportunity in Macau.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.800
He didn’t hesitate to bring in western games&nbsp;
that were far more predatory. He also invested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.640
significant amounts of money into developing&nbsp;
the maritime routes between mainland Asia and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.240
Macau which made the region more accessible than&nbsp;
ever. And before you knew it, Macau would become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.840
the Las Vegas of Asia. While Macau’s economic&nbsp;
problems were finally being solved, Portugal soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:39.280
had to deal with the Cultural Revolution aka the&nbsp;
Communist Revolution of China. Portugal saw loads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.240
of uprisings across Macau and while they tried to&nbsp;
control these using soldiers, the distance betwen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.720
Macau and Portugal made this quite difficult.&nbsp;
Soon enough, Portugal would find themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.120
asking for China’s help in controlling the region.&nbsp;
And eventually, this would result in them turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.800
over the entire region to China in 1999. And&nbsp;
that’s how the Macau we know today was created.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:03.200
CHINA TIGHTENING:&nbsp;

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:08.960
One of the biggest economic threats for Macau&nbsp;
is China. While China has yet to outright ban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:15.040
gambling in Macao, it’s no secret that China is&nbsp;
strongly against gambling. Eversince the Communist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:21.520
Party tookover in 1949, gambling has been&nbsp;
illegal in China. This includes overseas gambling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:27.360
as well, but in practice, China doesn’t generally&nbsp;
prosecute gambling. Instead, they prefer to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:33.040
another approach. They try to make gambling&nbsp;
as inaccessible as possible. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.000
the process of getting a visa to Macau is&nbsp;
extremely difficult for everyday citizens. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:44.080
is one of the reasons that Macau is so lucrative.&nbsp;
Only rich people are actually able to go there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:49.200
During regular times, Macau attracts 22 million&nbsp;
gamblers per year while Las Vegas attracts 25&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.800
million gamblers. Despite having fewer visitors,&nbsp;
Macau averages $28 billion in gambling revenue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:01.200
while Las Vegas averages $11.1 billion. Clearly,&nbsp;
China’s visa policies haven’t hurt Macau’s top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:07.040
line all that much, but this isn’t to say that&nbsp;
Macau is free from China’s control. If anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.840
China has been more controlling than ever as&nbsp;
Beijing has launched a full on gambling crackdown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.800
For example, they’ve been implementing facial&nbsp;
recognition software in Macau’s ATMS and limiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.360
withdrawal limits. They’ve even been considering&nbsp;
a digital currency to better track money trails to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:27.440
casinos. But why is the CCP doing all this right&nbsp;
now? Casinos are already getting crushed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:34.000
pandemic, why make it even harder on them? Well,&nbsp;
the answer is that the CCP is worried about losing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:40.160
control. Eversince the 1970s, China has become&nbsp;
more and more captilistic, and one of the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:45.440
examples of this is their toleration of Macau.&nbsp;
But, they’ve started to feel that they’ve given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:51.040
companies and businessmen way too much power and&nbsp;
influence. And the event that made this abundantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:56.080
clear to them was Jack Ma’s infamous speech in&nbsp;
late 2020. If you’re not familiar with Jack Ma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:01.760
he’s the founder of Alibaba and the Ant Group and&nbsp;
he used to be the richest person in China until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:07.440
he got on their bad side. You see, in late 2020,&nbsp;
he gave a speech in which he criticized the CCP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:13.360
He even started the speech with a disclaimer that&nbsp;
he’s probably wrong, but the CCP didn’t care all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:18.240
that much about his little disclaimer. Jack Ma&nbsp;
would go missing for the next three months and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:23.120
eversince then, Jack Ma has been in the process&nbsp;
of handing over his entire fortune to the CCP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.080
In fact, as I’m writing this script, it was just&nbsp;
announced that Jack Ma will cede control of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:34.080
Ant Group to the CCP. Aside from destroying Jack,&nbsp;
the CCP has decided to crackdown on capitalism as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:40.000
a whole which of course includes Macau. The recent&nbsp;
casino shutdowns are likely a side effect of this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.400
The last time China shut down casinos was at the&nbsp;
beginning of the pandemic in Febraury of 2020&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:50.240
when fears were at all time highs. But even&nbsp;
then, they only shut them down for 15 days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:55.680
This time, however, casinos have already been&nbsp;
closed for 3 weeks. Is this a mere coincidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:00.720
or is the CCP trying to show Macau who’s in&nbsp;
control? I’ll let you be the judge of that.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:05.120
THE COUNTDOWN:&nbsp;

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:10.000
Even if Macau survives all of these crackdowns&nbsp;
and shutdowns, they still have a massive timer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:15.360
looming over their heads. You see, when China&nbsp;
took over Macau in 1999, they only agreed to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.800
Macau autonomy for 50 years. Macau falls under&nbsp;
China’s one country two systems policy just like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:26.160
Hong Kong. The policy states that these regions&nbsp;
are politically part of mainland China. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:30.480
they have the freedom to operate under a different&nbsp;
economic system for a set period of time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.640
These regions are supposed to use this time&nbsp;
to morph to China’s ideals before they unite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:40.080
economic systems. But, given the current state&nbsp;
of Macau, they haven’t really made any progress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:46.720
in this realm. Macau is literally almost 3 times&nbsp;
as dependent on gambling as Las Vegas and this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:53.360
is after 23 years of morphing time. Clearly,&nbsp;
Macau doesn’t have any intention of changing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.920
but it looks like China might have different&nbsp;
plans. According to the initial agreement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:04.080
Macau will become one with China in 2049 which&nbsp;
means that gambling will become illegal. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:10.160
the general consensus has been that China wont&nbsp;
actually do anything after 2049. The reasoning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:15.600
is that Macau is simply so popular and profitable&nbsp;
that it doesn’t make sense to shut it down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:20.560
ruin the region. But, it looks like China&nbsp;
is moving to decouple Macau from gambling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.960
According to Wynn Macau chairman Allan Zeman,&nbsp;
“what Beijing wants, is to have a lot more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.360
non-gaming facilities.” And it seems like they’re&nbsp;
planning on leveraging the upcoming gambling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:34.240
license renewal at the end of this year as a&nbsp;
negotiating chip. Honestly, there’s no way, these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:40.320
licenses don’t get renewed, but it looks like&nbsp;
the CCP wants certain policies in place first.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:44.720
First, the CCP wants Macau to create a&nbsp;
special non-gaming zone. This zone will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:50.400
be dedicated to tech manufacturing, tourism,&nbsp;
medicine, conventions, and sports. Secondly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:55.840
the CCP wants shorter gambling licenses. Right&nbsp;
now, licenses last 20 years and renewals have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:01.200
to be made every 5 years after that. Moving&nbsp;
forward, however, the CCP wants 10 year licences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:06.080
followed by 3 year renewal periods. China also&nbsp;
wants reform regarding high risk gambling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:10.640
For example, they want to reduce the number of&nbsp;
slot machines each casino can own. All these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.520
reforms are designed to move Macau away from&nbsp;
gambling, but by the looks of the Macau economy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:20.960
right now, things aren’t progressing all that&nbsp;
well and that brings us to where we are today.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:25.360
THE FUTURE OF MACAU:&nbsp;

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:30.400
Looking forward, the state of Macau will really be&nbsp;
dependent on what casinos decide to do. How long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.320
will they be willing to put up with Chinese&nbsp;
politics before they decide to leave Macau?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.640
Under normal circumstances, this would be the&nbsp;
last thing they’d want to do given how profitable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:44.560
Macau is. However, most casinos are already&nbsp;
hurting quite a bit. Wynn resorts, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.280
hasn’t had a single profitable quarter since the&nbsp;
start of the pandemic. Fortunately, they still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:54.400
have quite a bit of cash on hand, but if does&nbsp;
come to shutting down a casino and scaling back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:59.040
Macau may very well be the victim. While&nbsp;
Macau is often the most profitable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.120
they’re also the most risky and&nbsp;
uncertain. So, when you’re scaling back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.080
you probably want to stick to areas that are more&nbsp;
stable and reliable like Las Vegas. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:13.520
we haven’t gotten to this point yet, but if China&nbsp;
continues to let Macau’s economy get destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.920
this may very well become a possibility.&nbsp;
And if casinos start leaving Macau,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:23.520
it won’t be long till Macau goes bankrupt, so it’s&nbsp;
in their best interest to keep casinos around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:29.120
And honestly, it’s in China’s best interest to&nbsp;
keep Macau around. But who knows, their interest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.360
for control may be greater than their interest&nbsp;
for preserving Macau. Do you guys think Macau&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:39.440
will survive China? Comment that down below. Also,&nbsp;
drop a like if hope that Taiwan survives China.&nbsp;&nbsp;

